  1041		This is a formalization-only construction theorem. Fix a polynomially small
  1042		function $\delta_Q(\eps)$. There is a function
  1043		$\delta_P(\eps,md/q)=\poly(\eps,md/q)$, in the corrected sum sense,
  1044		such that for every projective strategy passing with error $\eps$ and
  1045		every joint point family satisfying the conclusions of
  1046		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-10} with error $\delta_Q(\eps)$, the concrete POVM
  1047		\[
  1048			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}
  1049			=\hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
  1050			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},Z),\ell_Z}_{f_Z}
  1051			 \hat M^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
  1052		\]
  1053		has evaluated consistency defect at most $\delta_P(\eps,md/q)$ with that
  1054		joint point family, averaged over two independent line-point samples,
  1055		for every directed opposite placement. The line-error function is chosen
  1056		after $\delta_Q$ and its polynomial bound. This isolates the consistency
  1057		part of the preceding construction while retaining its defining
  1058		measurement; see \cite{gap:qpbt_subline-claims-line-marginal}.
  1059	\end{lemma}
  1060	\begin{proof}
  1061	\leanok
  1062	Condition on the first line having nonzero direction. The two completed
  1063	point-to-line marginal comparisons and heterogeneous pasting bound the
  1064	actual sandwich measurement on that law. Restore the discarded probability,
  1065	at most $1/(2q)$, and multiply the conditioned error by its retained mass.
  1066	Polynomial absorption and the independent unit defect bound give the result.
  1067	\end{proof}
